...of cicadas.

00:17:34.786 --> 00:17:35.946
And then...

00:17:36.406 --> 00:17:37.926
Two and a half hours in.

00:17:38.326 --> 00:17:40.426
Time for the third phone call.

00:17:41.806 --> 00:17:42.786
What will he do?

00:17:43.406 --> 00:17:44.346
Here it comes.

00:17:47.126 --> 00:17:48.966
It should be ringing. Yeah.

00:17:49.326 --> 00:17:50.036
Minamikawa.

00:17:51.946 --> 00:17:53.426
That came in so quietly.

00:17:54.346 --> 00:17:55.766
Hello? Hey there.

00:17:56.606 --> 00:18:03.846
- What's up? - Hello? What are you up to
today? - Nothing planned for later, but...

00:18:04.286 --> 00:18:06.186
I'm in Atsugi right now, though.

00:18:06.906 --> 00:18:07.646
Oh, right.

00:18:08.026 --> 00:18:08.806
On my way back.

00:18:09.646 --> 00:18:10.586
Um, there was a...

00:18:11.546 --> 00:18:12.846
death in the family.

00:18:15.226 --> 00:18:16.326
So I went home...

00:18:16.686 --> 00:18:18.666
and I ended up spending all my money.

00:18:19.146 --> 00:18:20.206
So I was hoping...

00:18:20.766 --> 00:18:23.386
you could lend me money for a payment.

00:18:24.246 --> 00:18:25.886
Oh. How much?

00:18:26.746 --> 00:18:27.246
100,000...

00:18:28.206 --> 00:18:29.026
Whoa...

00:18:31.146 --> 00:18:31.966
Ah...

00:18:32.766 --> 00:18:35.046
Okay... / He's asking for more.

00:18:36.126 --> 00:18:37.746
Could I maybe get 300,000?

00:18:38.106 --> 00:18:38.686
A huge help.

00:18:40.026 --> 00:18:43.846
"300k for what? For who?"
"Right... for my grandma."

00:18:44.326 --> 00:18:47.396
Your grandma? 300k for your grandma?

00:18:47.846 --> 00:18:49.766
Didn't your grandma just pass away?

00:18:50.146 --> 00:18:51.226
Yes.

00:18:51.546 --> 00:18:57.126
"What do you mean?" "We're short on
funds." "Think! Just tell me what for!"

00:18:57.966 --> 00:18:59.946
I'll lend it. Just tell me what for.

00:19:00.546 --> 00:19:03.486
"It's for..." "This is your chance!"
"...the funeral flowers."

00:19:05.166 --> 00:19:07.466
Not wanting to miss his chance, Takano...

00:19:08.226 --> 00:19:14.406
...abruptly kills off his grandma
and doubles down on his funeral scam.

00:19:16.666 --> 00:19:18.266
Whoa, whoa. A funeral scam.

00:19:18.606 --> 00:19:20.766
"Thank you so much." "Seriously?"

00:19:21.306 --> 00:19:27.106
He managed to get 300,000 yen from
Minamikawa. Amazing, Namikawa-san. And there's more.

00:19:27.846 --> 00:19:36.866
Also... for cigarettes, water, a bento...
if there's a convenience store, could you buy...

00:19:37.232 --> 00:19:38.160
...some for me?

00:19:38.386 --> 00:19:39.066
How shameless.

00:19:39.926 --> 00:19:40.746
What's with you?

00:19:41.086 --> 00:19:41.826
Huh?

00:19:42.246 --> 00:19:44.426
Of course he's mad.
What... What the hell?

00:19:44.766 --> 00:19:46.806
What the hell? What is that? I mean...

00:19:47.246 --> 00:19:49.926
It's for the wake.

00:19:52.546 --> 00:19:54.456
Cigarettes? -Cigarettes and a bento.

00:19:55.826 --> 00:19:57.786
Who are they for? You? -For my grandma.

00:19:58.846 --> 00:19:59.666
Your g-grandma?

00:20:02.086 --> 00:20:03.426
Okay, got it.

00:20:03.746 --> 00:20:06.546
Right. I'm a bit tied up right now.

00:20:07.366 --> 00:20:09.286
It's a bit of a pain. You'll come? Okay.

00:20:10.196 --> 00:20:10.906
So, um...

00:20:11.386 --> 00:20:13.526
When you get to Tanshō Station,

00:20:13.826 --> 00:20:15.986
give me another call.

00:20:16.366 --> 00:20:17.166
That's the plan.

00:20:17.526 --> 00:20:18.006
And so,

00:20:18.406 --> 00:20:21.686
he managed to guide them to the location.

00:20:22.646 --> 00:20:27.206
Next. - Hey, Takano here. - Hi. Got a
minute?

00:20:27.986 --> 00:20:28.976
Takano... So, uh...

00:20:30.126 --> 00:20:31.906
with, like, a gravure model...

00:20:33.626 --> 00:20:35.486
There's this get-together,

00:20:35.786 --> 00:20:39.206
They asked for people, so I thought of
you. - You change your tune? Huh?

00:20:39.966 --> 00:20:41.486
What time?
- Yes?

00:20:42.306 --> 00:20:43.566
What time?
- Well, um...

00:20:43.886 --> 00:20:46.466
Well, I'm already going.

00:20:47.246 --> 00:20:48.126
Really?
- Yeah.

00:20:48.866 --> 00:20:55.126
- Food? - No, we're supposed to buy a gift
and all chip in. - What kind of party is that?

00:20:55.466 --> 00:20:58.766
Okay. So can I just give you money for my
share?

00:21:01.250 --> 00:21:04.270
- Yeah, that's fine. - So you'll buy it? -
I'll take care of it.

00:21:04.770 --> 00:21:06.050
Got it. Right, right.

00:21:06.050 --> 00:21:08.193
- I'll get it. - Got it, okay. - So...

00:21:08.277 --> 00:21:10.063
Okay, got it.
Can you lend me the cash?

00:21:11.550 --> 00:21:13.590
Wait, 20k? 200k? I'll need 200,000.

00:21:14.584 --> 00:21:15.156
200,000?!

00:21:15.510 --> 00:21:16.520
What are you buying?

00:21:16.924 --> 00:21:18.496
I'll manage with 100k.

00:21:19.890 --> 00:21:20.910
We're splitting it?

00:21:21.473 --> 00:21:22.187
We'll split it.

00:21:22.930 --> 00:21:31.020
And so, he succeeded in getting the two of
them to come out.

00:21:31.330 --> 00:21:34.370
And now, we wait again.

00:21:36.640 --> 00:21:40.530
So that's 400k now.

00:21:42.180 --> 00:21:42.690
So dirty.

00:21:44.210 --> 00:21:47.730
Aaaah...

00:21:49.350 --> 00:21:52.190
Jeez...

00:21:53.930 --> 00:21:55.310
Visually, it's hilarious.

00:21:55.770 --> 00:21:59.270
It's getting ridiculous.
The wide shot is probably the best angle.

00:22:01.670 --> 00:22:04.230
As the sun began to set,

00:22:06.150 --> 00:22:09.670
Takano grew stressed by the poor
conditions.

00:22:10.420 --> 00:22:12.330
There's a futon.

00:22:13.590 --> 00:22:15.150
What do I do with this?

00:22:18.060 --> 00:22:21.510
Can I use this to pull something over?

00:22:24.060 --> 00:22:28.230
He found a pile of trash
left in a corner of the ruins.

00:22:29.230 --> 00:22:29.670
Ugh.

00:22:30.710 --> 00:22:31.170
Oh.

00:22:35.210 --> 00:22:36.670
Ah! I want that futon!

00:22:38.230 --> 00:22:44.510
You really do want a futon. And this
bucket... I guess it'll work.

00:22:45.110 --> 00:22:46.550
It's like a chair.

00:22:47.310 --> 00:22:49.270
Whoa.

00:22:50.170 --> 00:22:52.550
Ahh. Oh.

00:22:56.760 --> 00:22:58.550
So much more comfortable.

00:22:59.770 --> 00:23:06.630
What are we even watching? In this
hellscape, Takano has regained a shred of his humanity.

00:23:07.790 --> 00:23:10.400
I feel like some of my stress has
disappeared.

00:23:10.870 --> 00:23:11.410
What?

00:23:13.130 --> 00:23:13.430
This

00:23:18.150 --> 00:23:19.640
A picture! Yeah!

00:23:21.360 --> 00:23:21.660
Wow.

00:23:24.290 --> 00:23:25.210
Alright!

00:23:25.930 --> 00:23:26.230
Oh.

00:23:29.790 --> 00:23:30.110
Oh.

00:23:30.690 --> 00:23:32.730
Getting comfy, bit by bit.

00:23:34.100 --> 00:23:35.150
Here he comes.

00:23:35.550 --> 00:23:38.910
He's here! Whoa, he's huge. He's down.
Come on, notice him!

00:23:39.630 --> 00:23:44.330
The guy on the phone is desperate. He's
disappeared. That's why it's so quiet.

00:23:45.590 --> 00:23:46.970
He's right behind you!

00:23:47.700 --> 00:23:52.240
Hey! Wait, no, that's not... Oh, it is!

00:23:52.670 --> 00:24:01.410
I had no clue... At least make a sound!
Ouch. You looked pretty satisfied. How many times do I have to do this "ouch" routine?

00:24:03.010 --> 00:24:07.550
Ah, what a total waste. My arm hurts...
One minute.

00:24:08.970 --> 00:24:10.050
Aida from Sanshiro.

00:24:11.570 --> 00:24:13.360
Hello? It's Takano.

00:24:13.770 --> 00:24:16.150
Hey there. Aida-san, what are you up to
today?

00:24:16.550 --> 00:24:17.950
I'm in Asahikawa right now.

00:24:18.550 --> 00:24:23.330
Asahikawa... in Hokkaido. Sorry, I'm gonna
hang up for a sec.

00:24:23.770 --> 00:24:24.870
Wait, what? -Bye.

00:24:25.990 --> 00:24:26.570
Okay, bye.

00:24:26.930 --> 00:24:30.610
So, what are you up to today?

00:24:32.110 --> 00:24:33.510
Today? I'm in Hokkaido.

00:24:34.130 --> 00:24:34.770
Hokkaido?

00:24:35.510 --> 00:24:42.110
Yeah, for a gig. -Okay. -A gig. What are
you doing? Not everyone here. See?

00:24:42.430 --> 00:24:44.290
Where's the gig? Asahikawa, right?

00:24:45.010 --> 00:24:46.310
Asahikawa... Oh.

00:24:48.150 --> 00:24:49.130
Alright, my bad.

00:24:50.210 --> 00:24:51.450
Hokkaido, seriously?

00:24:53.270 --> 00:24:54.850
What's even in Hokkaido?

00:24:56.310 --> 00:24:57.330
Oh, come on.

00:24:58.910 --> 00:25:01.030
Seriously, this past hour was a bust.

00:25:01.550 --> 00:25:03.600
A complete waste of time.

00:25:05.580 --> 00:25:08.330
I feel like I could make some shoes with
this.

00:25:08.630 --> 00:25:09.990
Ah.

00:25:10.350 --> 00:25:12.330
Hey! It's all over your clothes!

00:25:12.790 --> 00:25:13.930
And...

00:25:14.630 --> 00:25:16.850
With tools he found in the garbage pile,

00:25:17.990 --> 00:25:23.470
The diaper comedian resumes his 'dignity
restoration'.

00:25:23.880 --> 00:25:27.530
This is all for my dignity. Yes.

00:25:31.202 --> 00:25:31.932
That was close.

00:25:33.272 --> 00:25:34.842
I was about to lose it.

00:25:40.662 --> 00:25:40.962
Oh.

00:25:42.062 --> 00:25:43.522
What'd he grab?

00:25:44.902 --> 00:25:47.622
Alright.

00:25:48.262 --> 00:25:51.862
Yes! So happy. What are these? Socks!

00:25:52.182 --> 00:25:53.142
So happy!

00:25:55.512 --> 00:26:00.322
Whoa, so much better. I get it now. So
comfy.

00:26:00.622 --> 00:26:05.042
Socks are way comfier than barefoot. I
totally disagree.

00:26:05.402 --> 00:26:05.882
Opposite.

00:26:10.022 --> 00:26:11.882
Se—

00:26:17.482 --> 00:26:20.542
—riously? What an expression.

00:26:20.902 --> 00:26:25.242
I've never done this, I can't move.

00:26:27.042 --> 00:26:28.222
That first step...

00:26:28.922 --> 00:26:29.342
Scary.

00:26:30.382 --> 00:26:30.762
Huh?

00:26:31.262 --> 00:26:32.372
This is the worst.

00:26:34.252 --> 00:26:35.932
No toilet, either?

00:26:40.072 --> 00:26:41.522
Seriously...?

00:26:43.502 --> 00:26:44.562
Oh, it's coming.

00:26:45.002 --> 00:26:46.182
Are you really?

00:26:47.072 --> 00:26:48.882
It's happening. This is nuts.

00:26:49.622 --> 00:26:51.942
This is nuts. What's the best position?

00:26:53.402 --> 00:26:56.182
Should I sit? We're about to see something
wild.

00:26:56.802 --> 00:27:02.542
Don't call this the highlight. Oh...

00:27:03.662 --> 00:27:04.402
I'm gonna pee.

00:27:05.602 --> 00:27:06.402
Seriously?

00:27:08.782 --> 00:27:10.722
Ahhh, it's coming...

00:27:12.252 --> 00:27:13.082
Oh, it's coming.

00:27:14.542 --> 00:27:15.142
Coming out.

00:27:15.502 --> 00:27:17.042
You're doing it standing up.

00:27:17.782 --> 00:27:18.082
Ah.

00:27:21.902 --> 00:27:23.822
Oh. It's there. Crap.

00:27:24.752 --> 00:27:25.262
It is.

00:27:42.702 --> 00:27:43.002
Oh.

00:27:43.872 --> 00:27:45.082
It's out...

00:27:45.382 --> 00:27:49.502
It's out. Oh no, I did it. I have a really
bad feeling.

00:27:50.062 --> 00:27:54.822
Whoa, it's a bat.

00:27:56.342 --> 00:27:59.142
Whoa, seriously, no way. I can't handle
this.

00:28:00.522 --> 00:28:02.202
I can't calm down at all.

00:28:02.682 --> 00:28:03.902
After seeing a bat.

00:28:04.772 --> 00:28:06.842
And there are so many. I saw one.

00:28:16.442 --> 00:28:17.262
What now?

00:28:17.602 --> 00:28:21.722
Oh, here it comes. Oh, this is fine. If
it's coming from that way, it's allowed.

00:28:22.762 --> 00:28:23.982
They're coming down.

00:28:24.422 --> 00:28:25.782
They really...

00:28:31.752 --> 00:28:33.572
...thought out these rules.

00:28:34.602 --> 00:28:40.302
What, a mountain path? This is way too
far! And it's terrifying!

00:28:40.556 --> 00:28:41.628
That's correct.

00:28:49.782 --> 00:28:50.902
For ¥300,000.

00:28:51.352 --> 00:28:54.682
There's a bridge.
After you cross it,

00:28:55.102 --> 00:28:56.602
go down the stairs,

00:28:57.852 --> 00:29:00.362
Down the stairs?
Yes, you'll find a building.

00:29:01.462 --> 00:29:02.202
So scary.

00:29:03.182 --> 00:29:04.822
It's there. So scary.

00:29:05.612 --> 00:29:07.602
No, this is just too scary.

00:29:08.002 --> 00:29:09.372
What the heck?

00:29:10.662 --> 00:29:12.022
Hey! Don't mess with me.

00:29:15.662 --> 00:29:16.762
Namikawa-san?

00:29:17.282 --> 00:29:17.882
Thank god.

00:29:19.462 --> 00:29:22.562
You came, Namikawa-san! Please, come in.

00:29:24.062 --> 00:29:29.102
What are you doing here? Help me!
This is absolutely terrifying.

00:29:33.314 --> 00:29:34.504
He must be so happy.

00:29:35.254 --> 00:29:40.874
"Ah, I see." "Don't 'I see' me!"
First off, thank you for coming.

00:29:41.374 --> 00:29:42.374
Catches on quick.

00:29:42.664 --> 00:29:44.164
Thanks for making the long trip.

00:29:44.714 --> 00:29:51.814
It was so far. - Thanks again. They just
gave me the address... Wait, is that guy in a diaper?

00:29:53.104 --> 00:29:54.614
So this isn't *Wed Downtown*?

00:29:55.504 --> 00:29:56.674
Would they go this far?

00:29:57.474 --> 00:30:00.454
Broadcast TV? - Sharp. / So it's not *Wed
Downtown*?

00:30:02.304 --> 00:30:06.894
So we're in diaper territory now. /
Meaning, no bathroom breaks.

00:30:08.054 --> 00:30:09.334
I've got nothing.

00:30:09.734 --> 00:30:12.814
Did you bring any money?

00:30:13.574 --> 00:30:16.774
- Yeah, I did. / - Sorry, that was a weird
question.

00:30:17.934 --> 00:30:20.574
- I brought 300k, just in case. / -
300,000?!

00:30:21.694 --> 00:30:25.054
Well, for drinks and stuff... / I figured
for you... um...

00:30:26.114 --> 00:30:28.924
Lunch, drinks, and cigarettes, right?

00:30:29.434 --> 00:30:32.204
You're a great senpai. -Cigarettes?
-Anything's fine.

00:30:32.768 --> 00:30:33.340
No lighter.

00:30:35.974 --> 00:30:36.364
Here.

00:30:37.434 --> 00:30:38.114
Really?

00:30:39.154 --> 00:30:40.004
Oh, for me?

00:30:41.454 --> 00:30:42.694
Huh? Are you mad?

00:30:43.714 --> 00:30:46.414
Just now. You got annoyed, right?

00:30:46.734 --> 00:30:49.214
No, wait. I drove for 2 hours, speeding
here...

00:30:49.554 --> 00:30:51.214
...to get annoyed at my senpai now?

00:30:51.904 --> 00:30:53.994
It wasn't like that.

00:30:54.394 --> 00:30:56.034
I've just been sitting here.

00:30:56.554 --> 00:30:57.374
Oh.

00:30:59.083 --> 00:31:01.225
Oh, tea. Thanks.
You haven't had any?

00:31:01.414 --> 00:31:02.714
It's okay, go ahead.

00:31:03.954 --> 00:31:06.334
Where'd you find this? It's amazing.

00:31:08.914 --> 00:31:10.124
It's so good.

00:31:11.654 --> 00:31:12.414
Mmm.

00:31:12.794 --> 00:31:19.254
You guys are the best. Seriously.

00:31:19.534 --> 00:31:20.034
Hey, mine!

00:31:21.334 --> 00:31:24.634
I was genuinely worried about you.
I'm so glad you're okay.

00:31:36.734 --> 00:31:41.234
Okay... Whoa! That's awesome.

00:31:41.854 --> 00:31:43.374
Thank you. It worked.

00:31:43.734 --> 00:31:44.614
That's great.

00:31:45.527 --> 00:31:47.741
Oh, change! Thank you. Thank you so much.

00:31:48.254 --> 00:31:49.074
I'll take...

00:31:52.474 --> 00:31:53.274
...this. Huh?

00:31:54.374 --> 00:31:58.454
Takano. Huh? What?

00:31:58.954 --> 00:31:59.414
Takano.

00:31:59.874 --> 00:32:03.014
What? Good morning. / - Good morning.

00:32:03.974 --> 00:32:04.294
Lied?

00:32:04.774 --> 00:32:05.574
Sorry.

00:32:07.234 --> 00:32:13.174
There's no way we'd have a mixer here. /
It's not that I tricked you, exactly.

00:32:14.724 --> 00:32:16.394
You're the worst.

00:32:17.294 --> 00:32:17.874
No, no.

00:32:18.320 --> 00:32:18.748
(Tch)

00:32:19.034 --> 00:32:23.514
I should've known. This is the absolute
worst. It can't get any worse.

00:32:24.834 --> 00:32:26.874
It's a 2 or 3 hour trip home.

00:32:27.734 --> 00:32:31.134
What kind of mixer is this?! A simple
'sorry' isn't enough.

00:32:34.074 --> 00:32:37.754
1,000 yen.

00:32:44.034 --> 00:32:44.654
Whoa.

00:32:48.034 --> 00:32:50.094
For real? I don't get it yet.

00:32:51.294 --> 00:32:53.814
Won 100,000 yen. Totaling 400,000...

00:32:54.134 --> 00:32:59.054
You came here all ready to get lucky,
bringing a ton of condoms.

00:33:00.344 --> 00:33:01.074
Cond...

00:33:01.454 --> 00:33:04.154
That's not happening here. I'm really
sorry.

00:33:06.994 --> 00:33:09.244
Could you put that down? / I'm Dousucchi.

00:33:10.294 --> 00:33:10.694
Oh.

00:33:12.684 --> 00:33:14.114
A cigarette?

00:33:14.251 --> 00:33:15.037
Thank you.

00:33:15.794 --> 00:33:16.974
Thanks.

00:33:17.756 --> 00:33:18.542
Thank you.

00:33:20.054 --> 00:33:21.174
I'm sorry.

00:33:22.014 --> 00:33:22.714
Whoa.

00:33:23.734 --> 00:33:24.334
It's huge.

00:33:25.694 --> 00:33:27.654
¥400k for the two of us. That's huge.

00:33:32.486 --> 00:33:33.566
This is where we're at.

00:33:35.496 --> 00:33:39.766
Two hours have passed since Shinichi got
home.

00:33:40.176 --> 00:33:42.626
And his phone negotiations have failed.

00:33:43.966 --> 00:33:45.066
Thanks anyway.

00:33:49.336 --> 00:33:51.206
What even is this segment?

00:33:53.266 --> 00:33:55.486
This is crazy, right? Yeah.

00:33:57.656 --> 00:34:01.936
This is nuts, seriously. It really is.
And then...

00:34:02.526 --> 00:34:03.966
Huh? What's this over here?

00:34:05.146 --> 00:34:07.806
Huh? "Ko"...

00:34:08.386 --> 00:34:09.966
What the heck?

00:34:11.726 --> 00:34:15.266
Whoa, what's this? He's starting to look
like he actually lives here.

00:34:15.646 --> 00:34:18.126
Who? What? Who? "Ko"? "Taiko"?
What is this?

00:34:19.566 --> 00:34:23.106
What is this? Naiko? Thanks. This is
terrifying.

00:34:23.926 --> 00:34:24.406
Come in.

00:34:25.086 --> 00:34:30.176
Is this really okay? / Yeah, come on in. /
Taiko, thank you.

00:34:31.926 --> 00:34:38.396
Appearing is a junior comedian from Linda
Color∞, who scrapes by working part-time.

00:34:39.066 --> 00:34:39.746
Taiko.

00:34:40.586 --> 00:34:42.726
Did you bring money? / I did.

00:34:43.053 --> 00:34:44.339
Thanks, thanks, thanks!

00:34:44.426 --> 00:34:46.066
I brought all the cash I had.

00:34:46.586 --> 00:34:48.486
50,000? / No, 180,000.

00:34:49.426 --> 00:34:50.906
You're lending me 180,000?

00:34:51.796 --> 00:34:53.526
Well, you said you needed help.

00:34:53.906 --> 00:34:55.626
You're so kind. Um...

00:34:55.966 --> 00:35:04.006
To help the struggling Takano, Taiko
scraped together what little money he had.

00:35:04.786 --> 00:35:05.386
So much cash.

00:35:12.286 --> 00:35:13.366
Thank you.

00:35:13.746 --> 00:35:16.626
Thanks. That makes 15,000 yen. Wow.

00:35:18.106 --> 00:35:18.886
Really, thanks.

00:35:19.946 --> 00:35:22.046
Wow, this helps more than I expected.

00:35:22.406 --> 00:35:22.886
Really.

00:35:23.386 --> 00:35:23.726
Pants.

00:35:24.666 --> 00:35:25.606
And finally...

00:35:26.246 --> 00:35:32.466
(Narrator) He also gets the underwear
Takano was wearing. - Huh? - That is weird.

00:35:33.386 --> 00:35:35.926
- That's crazy!
- I feel less like a prisoner.

00:35:36.446 --> 00:35:39.326
- You gave him your underwear?
- That's a surprising amount.

00:35:40.766 --> 00:35:41.966
That 180,000 yen...

00:35:43.766 --> 00:35:45.026
I'm so grateful.

00:35:46.576 --> 00:35:49.746
He was thinking about his junior,

00:35:50.326 --> 00:35:52.206
who came to his aid in a pinch.

00:35:52.866 --> 00:35:54.966
So scary. What is this? Who else is there?

00:35:55.386 --> 00:35:58.306
Takano? Takano?

00:35:58.606 --> 00:36:08.106
What is this? Seriously, what is this?
Tomoshige, who was supposed to be in Fukushima that day...

00:36:08.766 --> 00:36:11.046
...traveled 6 hours to get to Takano.

00:36:11.886 --> 00:36:13.446
I need... to borrow some money.

00:36:14.066 --> 00:36:17.526
No, seriously... I like you, Takano,

00:36:18.066 --> 00:36:21.906
and I respect you, but what is this?

00:36:22.526 --> 00:36:23.486
You have to explain.

00:36:24.286 --> 00:36:26.476
This is terrifying. I need a loan...

00:36:28.366 --> 00:36:29.386
...or I can't get out.

00:36:29.866 --> 00:36:31.086
And so...

00:36:32.126 --> 00:36:33.566
500,000 yen? Are you sure?

00:36:34.586 --> 00:36:35.826
Yeah, it's fine.

00:36:36.226 --> 00:36:41.146
I'm so sorry. 500,000 yen? Thank you so
much.

00:36:41.666 --> 00:36:43.426
This is money for my wife and kid.

00:36:43.786 --> 00:36:45.626
This is from our family savings.

00:36:46.386 --> 00:36:46.786
Please.

00:36:47.111 --> 00:36:49.111
I'm sorry. I will. I promise.

00:36:49.566 --> 00:36:51.196
Okay? Thank you.
-Good luck.

00:36:52.546 --> 00:36:54.126
This should be enough to get out.

00:36:54.546 --> 00:36:55.066
Right.

00:36:57.486 --> 00:36:58.406
So, did it work?

00:36:59.126 --> 00:37:01.866
50.

00:37:02.366 --> 00:37:03.666
Oh, so it worked? Wait,

00:37:03.986 --> 00:37:04.446
Amazing.

00:37:07.786 --> 00:37:08.706
Whoa. What's this?

00:37:09.226 --> 00:37:09.546
Huh?

00:37:09.886 --> 00:37:10.406
It's here.

00:37:16.286 --> 00:37:18.086
A key. Hmm. Where's the key?

00:37:20.006 --> 00:37:22.046
Here it is.

00:37:22.566 --> 00:37:23.806
Ah, I can get out.

00:37:24.256 --> 00:37:26.446
I can get out! We're out! Whoa!

00:37:26.806 --> 00:37:30.886
I made it out! Incredible!

00:37:33.602 --> 00:37:34.582
That was scary.

00:37:36.122 --> 00:37:37.032
That was close.

00:37:38.972 --> 00:37:39.882
What'd you think?

00:37:40.482 --> 00:37:41.882
See it all. It's hilarious.

00:37:43.202 --> 00:37:45.482
It's hilarious. Right? It really is.

00:37:45.862 --> 00:37:52.582
I've never seen footage like that.
Never seen someone pee in a diaper. Right?

00:37:52.962 --> 00:37:55.062
Rare footage.
And the 'Dignity Restore.'

00:37:56.662 --> 00:37:59.822
I've never heard that phrase before.
'Dignity Restore.'

00:38:00.142 --> 00:38:02.442
But you could never air that on TV, right?

00:38:03.082 --> 00:38:05.102
I'm amazed they got the OK to air this.

00:38:06.501 --> 00:38:07.143
We didn't.

00:38:07.832 --> 00:38:08.132
What?

00:38:10.002 --> 00:38:11.542
The network shot us down.

00:38:12.012 --> 00:38:12.312
On this.

00:38:13.042 --> 00:38:20.142
-What do you mean we can't air it? -It's
not up for debate. We can't broadcast that.

00:38:20.462 --> 00:38:21.982
What's wrong with it?

00:38:22.342 --> 00:38:27.022
The problem is that you, a producer,
think that's okay to air.

00:38:27.422 --> 00:38:36.922
-But we already shot it! What do I tell
their agencies? -You're the one who ignored our request and filmed that, Onigoe!

00:38:38.462 --> 00:38:40.642
What we asked for...

00:38:41.062 --> 00:38:44.222
...was a heartwarming prank show.

00:38:46.442 --> 00:38:51.642
They were asked for a "heartwarming prank
show" and made *that*? No wonder it was rejected.

00:38:53.002 --> 00:38:53.342
Please!

00:38:54.343 --> 00:38:54.701
What?

00:38:55.912 --> 00:38:57.442
I need a favor.

00:38:59.462 --> 00:39:00.382
Through editing,

00:39:01.122 --> 00:39:04.062
turn this footage into something
heartwarming.

00:39:04.602 --> 00:39:05.582
What?

00:39:12.442 --> 00:39:16.472
The footage is too absurd. There's no
reason for Takano to seem positive.

00:39:18.182 --> 00:39:24.902
When Takano gets jailed, he suddenly
starts resisting. It's weird. I'm thinking of changing the on-screen text there. Seriously.

00:39:26.742 --> 00:39:28.102
Let's do it!

00:39:28.582 --> 00:39:34.542
Oh man, this is gonna be hard.

00:39:34.902 --> 00:39:36.322
Okay, let's fix it like this.

00:39:39.692 --> 00:39:41.572
Music Station-style.

00:39:41.942 --> 00:39:46.042
Music Station. Can you do it?
This is serious, Koshi-san. Huh?

00:39:46.922 --> 00:39:49.702
If this doesn't air, the company will go
under.

00:39:53.392 --> 00:39:54.922
Will this be moving?

00:39:55.262 --> 00:39:57.762
I'll be moved.
- You won't. - What?

00:39:58.222 --> 00:40:01.122
Thanks for watching 'Tears from a Devilish
Prank'.

00:40:01.982 --> 00:40:04.902
So, how was it? Pretty fun, right?

00:40:05.300 --> 00:40:06.014
Amazing, huh?

00:40:06.362 --> 00:40:09.702
Fun, right? And this is just the start for
us.

00:40:09.873 --> 00:40:10.731
We'll be huge.

00:40:11.662 --> 00:40:13.442
They told us to make it heartwarming.

00:40:14.062 --> 00:40:15.082
That's what they said.

00:40:15.542 --> 00:40:18.982
Like I could do that! How would that even
work?

00:40:19.782 --> 00:40:25.752
To see the rest of 'Tears from the Demon
Prank,' sign up for DMM TV.

00:40:26.422 --> 00:40:28.542
For first-time subscribers to DMM TV,

00:40:28.862 --> 00:40:33.402
you get a 30-day free trial. So if you're
interested, please sign up!
